# EPG "Not Available" Placeholder — Design Review & Fix

## Context

The EPG panel renders a placeholder (`.epg-not-available`, [epg-list.component.scss:211-219](libs/ui/epg/src/lib/epg-list/epg-list.component.scss:211)) when no programmes exist for the selected date. The current treatment is a **dashed-bordered, rounded box** with the centered message *"Ooops, EPG is not available for the selected date"*. The user is questioning whether this fits the app's visual language.

## Verdict: it doesn't fit.

The placeholder is a one-off pattern that diverges from every other empty state in the codebase. Concrete issues:

| # | Issue | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Pattern inconsistency.** Every other empty state uses a centered icon + title + hint with **no border, no card shape**. | [groups-view.component.scss:236-278](libs/ui/components/src/lib/channel-list-container/groups-view/groups-view.component.scss:236), [season-container.component.scss:115](libs/ui/components/src/lib/season-container/season-container.component.scss:115), portal-empty-state component |
| 2 | **Wrong affordance signal.** A dashed border conventionally signals a *drop zone* or *"add-new" placeholder* — i.e. interactive. EPG-missing is passive/informational, so the stroke miscommunicates. | UX Wiki rule `ux-jakobs-familiar-patterns`, `ux-similarity-consistency` |
| 3 | **Visual weight wrong.** Empty states should recede; this one announces itself with a thick rounded stroke that competes with the program list above it. | UX Wiki `ux-pragnanz-simplify`, `ux-aesthetic-usability` |
| 4 | **Missing hierarchy.** Sibling empty states use a 1.05rem title + 0.85rem hint (two lines of meaning); this is one undifferentiated 0.88rem line. | [groups-view.component.scss:266-278](libs/ui/components/src/lib/channel-list-container/groups-view/groups-view.component.scss:266) |
| 5 | **No icon.** The convention in the codebase is a 48px Material icon at 0.5 opacity (`folder_off`, `search_off`). | [groups-view.component.html:3-5](libs/ui/components/src/lib/channel-list-container/groups-view/groups-view.component.html:3) |
| 6 | **Microcopy.** "Ooops" is misspelled (should be "Oops"), and the apologetic tone is inappropriate — EPG missing for a date is not a user error. The message also gives no next step. | UX Wiki `ux-peak-end-finish-strong` |
| 7 | **Concentric-radius mismatch.** 12px radius matches the *program-item* card, so the empty state reads as a single oversized card rather than a panel-spanning state. | UX Wiki `visual-concentric-radius` |

The dashed box is the kind of placeholder you scaffold during early development and then never come back to — the rest of the app has clearly moved past this style.

## Recommended fix — match the existing empty-state pattern

Drop the dashed box. Reuse the `.groups-view-empty-state` shape (icon + title + hint, centered in the panel). This is the smallest possible change that resolves all seven issues at once.

### Template change — [epg-list.component.html:107-111](libs/ui/epg/src/lib/epg-list/epg-list.component.html:107)

```html
@} @else {
    <div class="epg-empty-state">
        <mat-icon class="empty-state-icon">event_busy</mat-icon>
        <div class="empty-state-title">
            {{ 'EPG.NO_GUIDE_TITLE' | translate }}
        </div>
        <div class="empty-state-hint">
            {{ 'EPG.NO_GUIDE_HINT' | translate }}
        </div>
    </div>
}
```

(`mat-icon` import already used elsewhere in the file via the date navigator's `chevron_left`/`chevron_right`.)

### SCSS change — [epg-list.component.scss:211-219](libs/ui/epg/src/lib/epg-list/epg-list.component.scss:211)

Replace the `.epg-not-available` block with:

```scss
.epg-empty-state {
    flex: 1;
    min-height: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 40px 24px;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--app-muted-color);

    .empty-state-icon {
        width: 48px;
        height: 48px;
        font-size: 48px;
        opacity: 0.5;
        margin-bottom: 16px;
    }

    .empty-state-title {
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        font-weight: 520;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
        margin-bottom: 8px;
        text-wrap: balance;
    }

    .empty-state-hint {
        opacity: 0.65;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        max-width: 240px;
        line-height: 1.4;
        text-wrap: pretty;
    }
}
```

Tokens, font sizes and opacities are copied verbatim from the existing pattern so the two empty states render at identical visual weight.

### i18n changes

- Reuse the existing key `EPG.EPG_NOT_AVAILABLE_DATE` for the **title**, but rewrite the EN copy from *"Ooops, EPG is not available for the selected date"* → *"No program guide"* (also fixes the typo). Other locales need a one-line copy update; many already use a softer tone (e.g. `fr`, `it`, `nl`, `ko`, `ja`).
- Add a new key `EPG.NO_GUIDE_HINT` for the hint line, e.g. *"Try a different date or refresh the playlist."*
- 18 locale files in [apps/web/src/assets/i18n/](apps/web/src/assets/i18n/) need the new hint key (English first; others can be added incrementally — `ngx-translate` falls back to the key string if a locale lacks it).

## Critical files

- [libs/ui/epg/src/lib/epg-list/epg-list.component.html](libs/ui/epg/src/lib/epg-list/epg-list.component.html) — swap the placeholder block
- [libs/ui/epg/src/lib/epg-list/epg-list.component.scss](libs/ui/epg/src/lib/epg-list/epg-list.component.scss) — replace `.epg-not-available` with `.epg-empty-state`
- [apps/web/src/assets/i18n/en.json](apps/web/src/assets/i18n/en.json) — new copy + new `NO_GUIDE_HINT` key (mandatory)
- 17 other locale files — same key additions (can be batched or staged)

Reference patterns to copy from:
- [libs/ui/components/src/lib/channel-list-container/groups-view/groups-view.component.html:1-22](libs/ui/components/src/lib/channel-list-container/groups-view/groups-view.component.html:1) — template shape
- [libs/ui/components/src/lib/channel-list-container/groups-view/groups-view.component.scss:236-278](libs/ui/components/src/lib/channel-list-container/groups-view/groups-view.component.scss:236) — token values

## Skipped / not in scope

- No JS/component-class change is needed — this is template + styles + i18n only.
- No regression risk to EPG fetching or date navigation logic.

## Verification

1. **Visual sanity**, light + dark theme:
   - `pnpm run serve:backend` (Electron) → open an Xtream playlist → live channel with EPG → click `chevron_left` until landing on a date with no EPG. Confirm the empty state renders centered with icon, title, hint, and matches the visual language of the groups/categories empty state.
   - Toggle dark/light theme; confirm `--app-muted-color` and icon opacity look right in both.
2. **Truncation / responsive**: drag the EPG drawer narrower; confirm the 240px `max-width` hint wraps cleanly without scroll.
3. **i18n fallback**: temporarily switch app language to one without `NO_GUIDE_HINT`; confirm `ngx-translate` shows the raw key (acceptable as a fallback) and doesn't break layout.
4. **No automated test for visual changes** is required per the project's test-impact policy in `CLAUDE.md` — this is a styling change with no behavior shift, so unit/E2E coverage stays as-is. Manual CDP verification is sufficient. Document that decision in the final task summary.

## Open question

If you'd rather keep the bordered "card" feel (e.g. you intentionally want it to feel framed), an alternative is to keep the box but replace `dashed` with a 1px **solid** `var(--app-separator)` and add the icon-title-hint stack inside it. This is hybrid — fixes affordance and hierarchy issues but keeps the inconsistency with the rest of the empty states. I do not recommend it, but flag it in case the dashed look was a deliberate visual choice rather than an early scaffold.

